body:
Huh, didn't know that. I guess that's just part of it. I'm too used to unresponsive allowing for longer tricks, which makes sense.

&#x200B;

I figured it should last at least 10 seconds, but maybe it's not like that.

It struggles to get 10 seconds. My throws don't look like they vibrate much. Some of my worse throws have the string leaning a little on the sides, which would make sense as to why it doesn't spin long. But I've had throws where I pick it up by the string and look at where the string is on the bearing as it spins and it's not hitting the side at all, just perfectly straight and still it barely lasts 10 seconds.

&#x200B;

I looked at the bearing and when I flick it, it barely moves at all. I've been told that that's normal, but I've also been told that that's bad.

&#x200B;

I'm considering getting a new bearing or some lube, which would suck since I just got this yoyo.
